ect defense around the  grave site  but recently that relationship has  broken down due to disagreements over  how to proceed with that work  Sue Valley had planned to conduct field  work in the fall of 2022 to identify  where the fence should go but Mark  denied them entry to the property  all we're asking for  the vanity  Sioux Valley Dakota Nation Chief  Jennifer bone says all levels of  government need to help communities  access and commemorate these sacred  sites  we didn't create these problems right  but now if we want  something done then it's up to us to do  that which I don't think is fair  [Music]  and this will have been where my  grandmother was taken  feels strange to be going somewhere  where she would have come as a young  very very young child  before relocating to England Melanie  bagley's grandmother lived on a reserve  Northeast of Winnipeg and attended  Brandon residential school  on this day Melanie and her brother are  visiting the former School site for the  first time  Melanie was unaware of her indigenous  Heritage until she was in her 20s  since then she's been on a journey to  learn more about her family's ancestry  that I said to my grandmother  what was it like growing up on the  reserve and what was it like going to  residential school  so gentle soft-spoken woman and she just  turned to me she said  we never talk about that  and it was like  okay I don't know what that means but I  must never ever ever ask her again  and she didn't but she remained curious  while researching her grandmother's  school life she stumbled upon an unknown  part of her family history  her grandmother had a younger sister  Lina who also went to the school  when I found that I had like a shock  well I've never heard of her so I spoke  to another cousin and another cousin and  nobody's ever heard of her  and so  who who is she where where did she go  and what has it been like for you  discovering that you have this great  aunt that you you never knew you had 